{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The platform's own recorded distances put this deviation at exactly the tolerance line: 8.3 km actual less 7.3 km recommended is 1.00 km, and POL-RD-22 provides that a deviation of 1.0 km or less is within tolerance. The trip record's derived deviation block returns deviation_km 1.00 with within_tolerance true, so nothing is refundable on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.within_tolerance",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The traffic record does not justify this reroute, and that is the driver's friend here: the LTA advisory for the recommended Seletar Road segment is type NONE — no incident, roadwork or closure, speed bands 5-6 throughout — so under POL-RD-23 the reroute is not traffic-justified. The row of POL-RD-24 that then applies is row (e), 'not traffic-justified, deviation 1 km or less', which expressly yields no refund and leaves the present state standing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05007-01", "EV-TRIP-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-RD-23"],
      "relies_on": "derived.v7.justifies_reroute",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome is the same whichever way the traffic question falls, which is what makes this case safe to rule: under POL-RD-24(c) a traffic-justified reroute where the rider was not informed and the deviation is 1 km or less also produces no refund, and under POL-RD-24(e) an unjustified reroute at 1 km or less produces no refund. Both tolerance rows pay nothing, so no reading of the justification can turn a 1.00 km deviation into a refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05007", "EV-ADVIS-05007-01", "EV-CHAT-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider cannot use the GPS trace to stretch the distance in his favour. The trace itself measures only 6.996 km over 34 fixes, and POL-RD-22 is explicit that the trace shows which route was taken and when but is not used to re-measure distance, because a sparse trace understates a route's length. The deviation therefore stands at the platform's recorded 1.00 km, not at any figure the trace might suggest.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05007", "EV-TRIP-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even on the rider's own case the sum is far smaller than he asks for. The only money POL-RD-24 ever moves on a deviation is the excess distance fare — deviation distance times fare_breakdown.per_km_rate_sgd, without surge — which on a 1.00 km deviation at 0.72 SGD/km is 0.72 SGD, not the 2.50 SGD claimed. The claimed figure has no basis in the matrix.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05007", "EV-TRIP-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "NO_ACTION is party-relative, and on this record it runs for the driver. The rider is the filing party, and the payments ledger shows the 12.65 SGD metered fare as CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00; under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION means the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands, so the fare stays where it is rather than being returned.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log is empty — 0 messages, contiguous, matching the trip record — and the trip record carries no in-app calls, so the driver cannot establish that he notified the rider of the reroute as POL-RD-21 requires, and a verbal notice with no recording cannot be established. That omission does not open a refund on these facts: POL-RD-24's two tolerance rows, (c) for an uninformed rider and (e) for an unjustified reroute, pay nothing where the deviation is 1 km or less, and no row of the matrix conditions a refund on notification below that line.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05007", "EV-TRIP-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.message_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No escalation is forced on the routing question. The contested amount is 2.50 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band in which an AI ruling is final, and neither profile snapshot carries a fraud_flags entry of 1 or more, so no 0.95 threshold is engaged; under POL-RD-25 the ruling stands at 0.80 or more confidence, and the 2 km limb that clause describes is not in force on this record (ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false, and the trip record's derived block marks over_ai_limit false).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05007", "EV-RPROF-05007", "EV-DPROF-05007"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-RD-25"],
      "relies_on": "dispute.amount_contested_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on this record is impaired: the trip record, GPS trace, chat log, fare ledger, both profile snapshots and the LTA advisory are all COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes fired. There is therefore no gap in the evidence that could carry POL-GEN-26's escalation, and the deviation distance, the route taken and the justification are each established on the artifacts above.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05007", "EV-GPS-05007", "EV-CHAT-05007", "EV-FARE-05007", "EV-ADVIS-05007-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.93,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the fare stands and nothing is refunded. The platform's trip record (EV-TRIP-05007) shows the recommended route was Yishun Avenue 2, Yishun Avenue 1, Seletar Road, Sengkang West Avenue at 7.3 km, and the driver actually ran Yio Chu Kang Road and Jalan Kayu to a recorded 8.3 km. Under POL-RD-22 the deviation is 8.3 km minus 7.3 km = 1.00 km, and that clause provides that a deviation of 1.0 km or less is within tolerance. At 1.00 km the trip is at the tolerance line, and the line is inclusive, so the deviation is within tolerance. On justification, the only traffic data for the recommended Seletar Road segment during the trip window (EV-ADVIS-05007-01) is type NONE, with no congestion, incident, roadwork or closure (speed bands 5-6 throughout), so the reroute is not traffic-justified under POL-RD-23 and the driver's stated reason, that Jalan Kayu is smoother, is not a justification the policy recognises. POL-RD-24(e) therefore governs: a reroute that is not traffic-justified with a deviation of 1 km or less yields no refund and the present state stands. To the rider: your $2.50 request cannot be met. Even if a refund row were reached, POL-RD-24 pays only the excess distance fare, which on a 1.00 km deviation at the $0.72 per-km rate (EV-FARE-05007) is 1.00 x 0.72 = $0.72, not $2.50; rows (b) and (d), which pay that fare, require a deviation over 1 km, and this one is not over. Your point that the distances are rounded to 0.1 km and could conceal a true deviation above 1.0 km does not open an escalation under POL-GEN-26: POL-RD-22 fixes the measurement to the platform's recorded distances, and both are present, complete and unimpaired at weight 1.0, so the clause's own test runs and returns 1.00 km within tolerance. The empty chat log (EV-CHAT-05007) and the absence of any call recording do show the driver did not inform you of the deviation as POL-RD-21 requires, and that omission is noted; but no row of the POL-RD-24 matrix conditions a refund on notification where the deviation is within tolerance. To the driver: the notification failure under POL-RD-21 is a matter of record against you, though it changes nothing here because the deviation is within tolerance. Nothing escalates: the contested amount is $2.50, below POL-GEN-22's $10.00 AI-final threshold, no fraud flag is recorded, the 2 km limb of POL-RD-25 is not in force (ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false and over_ai_limit is false), and POL-RD-25's 0.80 confidence bar is met. Party profiles were not used to decide the trip, per POL-GEN-01. All artifacts are COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0; confidence is returned at 0.93. The $12.65 metered fare (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00) stands."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

